  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "sanitize_shallow",
    "file": "harfbuzz/src/hb-open-type.hh",
    "description": "`ArrayOf<Type, LenType>::sanitize_shallow()` passes `sizeof(Type)` as the `len_size` argument to `hb_sanitize_context_t::check_array_sized()`, although `len_size` is supposed to describe the array's count field (`LenType`). For `ArrayOf<HBGlyphID16, HBUINT32>` in cmap format 10, `sizeof(Type)` is 2, so `check_array_sized()` takes its unchecked multiplication path instead of the overflow-checked path required for a 32-bit count. A count of 0x80000000 multiplied by the 2-byte glyph size wraps to zero, allowing the truncated array to pass sanitization. Later `CmapSubtableTrimmed<HBUINT32>::collect_unicodes()` trusts the original count and reads `glyphIdArray[i]` beyond the heap blob.",
    "conditions": "A crafted font must expose a cmap format 10 trimmed subtable whose 32-bit `glyphIdArray.len` causes `len * 2` to wrap (the PoV uses 0x80000000), while providing far fewer glyph entries. In this PoV, the malformed SFNT directory exposes a 42-byte cmap blob starting at file offset 2; its encoding record points to a format 10 subtable at cmap offset 6, with count 0x80000000 and only about 16 bytes of glyph-array payload. The sanitizer erroneously validates a zero-byte wrapped range. `hb_face_collect_unicodes()` then dispatches to `CmapSubtableTrimmed<HBUINT32>::collect_unicodes()`, which iterates the attacker-controlled count and performs the out-of-bounds 2-byte read."
  },
